<%# The environment banner, on every page of the component demo.

    This is what replaced the purple nav row. The signal both are carrying is "this is not part of the
    product", and a nav row has nothing but colour to say it with, which is why it ended up as the loudest
    thing in a sidebar whose colour already means "you are here". A page can use a sentence.

    That is where the field puts it: Stripe's test mode banners the page rather than recolouring the
    navigation, GitLab's environment ribbon sits on the page chrome, and GOV.UK's phase banner - the closest
    documented match, since it exists to say "this thing is not the finished product and here is what that
    means for you" - sits above the page's own heading. So does this one.

    Three decisions in it:

    - **It names the environment rather than hard-coding one.** In the test suite it reads "Test
      environment", which is true, and it cannot go stale if the guard changes. Same reasoning as deriving a
      summary from its contents rather than restating it.
    - **`:warning`, not `:info`.** Amber is the field's colour for "you are not in the real thing" - Stripe's
      test mode, GitLab's non-production ribbon - and one line here is a genuine caution rather than a fact:
      the examples are real records out of this database. Measured on its own tint, amber-900 is 8.75:1 and
      amber-800 6.84:1.
    - **No dismiss, and no auto-hide.** The environment is still true in a minute. This repo's rule is that
      only an *outcome* removes itself; a banner describing the state of the page does not.

    It replaced a hand-rolled blue panel on the index page - `bg-blue-50 border border-blue-200 rounded-lg`
    with its own icon sizing - which said the components "will be used across all admin resource pages",
    written when they were new and long since true. Hand-rolling this panel is what `components/ui/_callout`
    was extracted to stop, and the index was the third instance. %>
<% body = "This page is a reference for the admin components, not part of the product. Its route exists " \
          "only in development and test, and the examples below are rendered from real records in this " \
          "database." %>

<%= render "components/ui/callout",
           tone: :warning,
           icon: "flask-conical",
           title: "#{Rails.env.capitalize} environment",
           body: body,
           testid: "environment-banner",
           class: "mb-6" %>
